! 1. Diaspora "aspects"

The three largest messages one research spirit wrote, ''held verbatim and unedited''. Its own words decide the heading above.

⚠ ''FENCED ON PURPOSE.'' Raw transcript carries `<<~`, `>>` and code fences of its own; unfenced it would read as GRAMMAR and corrupt the carrier that holds it. The fence makes every mark inside it ''content'' — the same law the corpus keeps for a quoted sigil: //an edge inside a fence is a lesson, never a link//.

<<~/ahu>>

